-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The MIT licence above covers the Fortelia application code only. The files
also bundle the following third-party material, each under its own licence:

1. Salamander Grand Piano samples
   Author: Alexander Holm. Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 3.0 (CC BY 3.0)
   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/
   Sample set as prepared by the Tone.js project (https://github.com/Tonejs/audio).
   The samples were compressed and embedded in the HTML file.

2. three.js
   Copyright (c) 2010-2026 three.js authors. Licence: MIT.
   https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js

3. WebXR Input Profiles: generic-hand models (left.glb, right.glb)
   Copyright Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates. Licence: MIT.
   https://github.com/immersive-web/webxr-input-profiles

4. Full classical pieces: scores from the Mutopia Project
   (https://www.mutopiaproject.org), converted to MIDI. The compositions are
   in the public domain. The typeset scores carry these licences:
   - Public domain: Für Elise (Stelios Samelis), Rondo alla Turca (Rune Zedeler
     and Chris Sawer), Prelude in C BWV 846 (Tobias Erbsland), Minuet in G
     (Allen Garvin), Chopin Preludes Op. 28 No. 4 and No. 7 (Magnus
     Lewis-Smith), Fantaisie-Impromptu (Guy D. Lederfein), Clair de lune and
     Arabesque No. 1 (Keith OHara), The Entertainer (Chris Sawer), In the Hall
     of the Mountain King (Coyau), Clementi Sonatina Op. 36 No. 1 (Brian D.
     Rude), Burgmüller Arabesque (Bas Wassink), Brahms Waltz Op. 39 No. 15
     (Brian D. Rude).
   - CC BY-SA 2.5: Moonlight Sonata, 1st movement, typeset by Stewart Holmes.
   - CC BY-SA 3.0: Sonata K545, 1st movement, typeset by Alejandro Sierra;
     Invention No. 1, typeset by jeff covey.
   - CC BY 3.0: Liszt Consolation No. 3, typeset by Ryan Prince.
   These MIDI files are adaptations of those editions and are shared under the
   same licences as the editions they come from.
